wgestures (2.1.2ubuntu1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Display shortcuts in familiar Ctrl+C notation in both settings interfaces.
  * Accept Ctrl+C, Control+C, Ctrl C and legacy <Control>c input formats.
  * Normalize saved shortcuts consistently across the Wayland and X11 backends.
  * Add Smart Copy, using Ctrl+Shift+C in terminals and Ctrl+C elsewhere.
  * Add Smart Paste, using Ctrl+Shift+V in terminals and Ctrl+V elsewhere.
  * Add a 35-degree fallback tolerance for imprecise single-direction gestures.
  * Simplify fresh-install defaults to right-up Smart Copy and right-down Smart Paste.

 -- WGestures Contributors <Ying@YingDev.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0800

wgestures (2.1.1ubuntu1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Force xz compression for Ubuntu 18.04 dpkg compatibility.
  * Keep the GNOME 46 Wayland and Python 3.6 X11 payload unchanged.

 -- WGestures Contributors <Ying@YingDev.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:35:00 +0800

wgestures (2.1.0ubuntu1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Add a Python 3.6 compatible X11 backend for Ubuntu 18.04 and Kali Xfce.
  * Add GTK3 preferences, session auto-selection and portable diagnostics.
  * Keep GNOME Shell 46 Wayland integration in the universal Debian package.

 -- WGestures Contributors <Ying@YingDev.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0800

